{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"22 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,14.225,3.651,3.268,"Britannia"],[13.889,14.731,30.952,2.373,2.124,"Volume is back; the margin is not"],[13.889,20.845,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Britannia fell 3.9% the day after its Q2 FY27 results and is 1.6% below the pre-"],[13.889,22.289,52.992,1.809,1.634,"results close, while the NIFTY rose 5.2%. At ₹4,900 it is 21% below its January"],[13.889,23.733,52.934,1.809,1.634,"high and trades on 44x FY27E and 39x FY28E EPS, the bottom of its three-year"],[13.889,25.177,52.966,1.809,1.634,"range of 39-67x forward earnings. The quarter was the largest in its history:"],[13.889,26.621,52.966,1.809,1.634,"sales rose 16.6% to ₹5,542 cr on 13% volume growth. Profit did not keep up:"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"EBITDA rose 7% and profit 10%. We rate the shares Neutral with a Dec-27"],[13.889,29.509,25.071,1.809,1.634,"target of ₹5,460, 11% above the price."],[13.889,31.995,52.951,1.809,1.634,"The volume came off a base that fell 3% around last September’s GST change."],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Gross margin fell 200bp to 39.6% as palm oil (+17%), milk (+16%), laminate"],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"(+18%) and fuel (+45%) rose year on year against 3.5% of pricing. More"],[13.889,36.328,52.934,1.809,1.634,"increases, mostly grammage cuts on ₹5 and ₹10 packs, take about two months"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"and will trim volume. EBITDA margin fell to 18.3% from 19.7%. We put the H2"],[13.889,39.216,52.936,1.809,1.634,"margin at 18.0% (18.9% a year ago) and FY27E EPS at ₹110.78 against"],[13.889,40.684,52.964,1.809,1.634,"consensus ₹112.42, +9% on FY26 EPS of ₹101.22 excluding a ₹95 cr tax-"],[13.889,42.128,52.931,1.809,1.634,"provision reversal. FY28E assumes the margin recovers to 18.3%: EPS ₹126.44"],[13.889,43.572,35.151,1.809,1.634,"against ₹127.78, down from ₹130.12 ninety days ago."],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"The target averages 53x, Britannia’s own three-year average, on EPS for the"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"twelve months after Dec-27 (₹137.2), or ₹7,244, and a ten-year FCFE DCF at an"],[13.889,48.946,52.936,1.809,1.634,"11% cost of equity and 6.5% terminal growth plus net cash, or ₹3,677 (₹4,696 at"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"10%). The legs are far apart: the multiple leg alone is +48%; the DCF needs free"],[13.889,51.834,52.964,1.809,1.634,"cash flow to grow 14.1% a year to FY37 against our 9.2%. The peer median of"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"36.7x gives ₹5,027; consensus is ₹5,702 (33 analysts, 23 buy). We would be"],[13.889,54.722,52.962,1.809,1.634,"wrong if pricing restores a 19% margin by FY28 with volume intact, earning"],[13.889,56.167,52.962,1.809,1.634,"back the old multiple. The main risk is the reverse: inflation outrunning pricing"],[13.889,57.611,30.402,1.809,1.634,"just as Reliance enters biscuits in Tamil Nadu."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,68.709,2.306,1.022,0.915,"4,500"],[14.451,66.942,2.306,1.022,0.915,"5,000"],[14.451,65.174,2.306,1.022,0.915,"5,500"],[14.451,63.407,2.306,1.022,0.915,"6,000"],[14.451,61.639,2.306,1.022,0.915,"6,500"],[17.913,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.539,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.326,69.404,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.08,69.404,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.959,70.575,2.601,1.275,1.111,"BRIT ("],[21.563,70.601,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.176,70.575,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.26,70.575,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.481,71.735,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.166,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.081,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.735,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.8,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[18.98,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−17.4%"],[24.247,72.8,2.26,1.387,1.209,"4.1%"],[28.028,72.8,3.394